From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: remove the dead level-order tree walker and stop citing it

The association-state tree builder (topology_build_tree_from_assoc)
replaced the level-order walker during the 2026-08 topology work, and
the old machinery kept compiling with zero callers - verified: nothing
references topology_build_tree, build_local_controller_root,
topology_num_devs, topology_num_agent_devs, nor the walker-only static
helpers (clear_backhaul_tree_relations, set_device_child_neighbors,
set_next_level_neighbors, find_neighbor_local_iface, is_wifi) outside
their own definitions - the last two fell out as -Werror=unused once
the walker went. The 2026-08-04
review flagged the cluster (finding 2.6) and two comments that still
presented the dead walker as the authority (finding 2.7): the
db_restore note and the sync-dispatch note now name
topology_build_tree_from_assoc, which is what actually runs, and a
sweep mislabelled as another patch is described by what it does.

Behaviour: none. Text and dead code only; the linked binary loses the
unreachable walker.
